The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. Build and tests were already green from the harness check at the start of this session; I didn't re-run the full suite.

One mistake to clean up: session_plan/ is gitignored, so the commit command in my instructions does nothing there. I force-added the file anyway, then made a second commit to take it back out of git. The file is still on disk for the planner. History now has two extra local commits: one that adds the file and one that removes it. Both are unpushed and can be squashed away. I didn't reset, because that would have meant asking first.

What I found by running things:
• Startup hang (#1052, first item): a project .yoyo.toml with system_file pointing at a pipe (a FIFO) makes yoyo -p hang until the 10-second timer kills it (exit 124, no output). The same setup with an ordinary file answers PONG in 1.8s. The bad line is src/cli.rs:1005. The fix is to read through the existing pipe-safe helper (read_regular_to_string), and cli.rs has 36 lines of room under its size limit. I only read the other two items in #1052 (--continue restore and the write_file diff preview); I didn't run them.
• Wrong exit codes (#982): doctor zzz, help zzz and update zzz all exit 0, and init zzz exits 0 and writes YOYO.md anyway. config show on a pipe .yoyo.toml prints the error but still exits 0.
• Data loss (#1053): at src/commands_todo.rs:770, an evidence.md that can't be read is treated as empty, then overwritten with one line, and the command reports green "Added evidence". I confirmed this by reading the code, not by running it.

Recent history: the last 10 sessions each completed 2 of 2 tasks, with no reverts, no CI failures in 14 days and no provider errors. The last four evolve runs succeeded.

Research: I saved a new note to yopedia.
• Fixes we already have: yoagent 0.25.8, which we're already on, ships two fixes from our reports: pipe-safe file tools (#341) and bash no longer waiting on a background job that holds its output (#342). The second should fix the same hang for helper agents (the sibling of #1049), but I haven't checked it through yoyo yet.
• Dead issue numbers: the Day 232 journal points to "#1050" and "#1051", which don't exist in this repo; they were moved to yoagent as #341 and #342. Nothing in src/ or the docs cites them, so only the journal is affected.
• Rivals: Claude Code and Codex spent this week on the same hardening work we're doing (output pipes held open by background jobs, config writes surviving early exit, resume keeping its state). Where they're ahead on features: Codex lets you send a follow-up to steer a turn while it's still answering, and it runs read-only tools in parallel.
• Write risk: our config and memory saves use a plain std::fs::write that truncates the file first, so a kill mid-save would leave it cut short. That's from reading the code; I didn't test it.

Suggested order for the planner: #1052, then #1053, then either the config show exit code (#982) or #1045. Watch the size limits: config.rs has 11 lines of room and commands_risk_unhittable.rs has 14.
